    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d300">

                <pb facs="0502" n="406" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg406"/>

                <head>No. 300.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Nelson to Mr. Fish</hi>,</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-03-25"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 25, 1872</date>.
                        (Received April 12.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 533.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a copy of a
                    dispatch from the United States vice-consul at Zacatecas, Anthony M. Kimball,
                    esq., dated the 11th instant, in which the late important military operations in
                    that vicinity are described with interesting particulars not generally
                    known.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>THOMAS H. NELSON.</signed>
                </closer>


                <xi:include href="d300-a1.xml" xpointer="d300-a1"/>
            </div>
